<h2>One after another</h2>
<p><code>im-stagger</code> on a parent numbers its children; every entrance reads that number as a delay (<code>--im-stagger</code>, 60ms a step).</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-auto im-stagger im-grid-sm" data-replay>
	<div class="im-card" data-im-in="rise"><span class="im-card-title">One</span></div>
	<div class="im-card" data-im-in="rise"><span class="im-card-title">Two</span></div>
	<div class="im-card" data-im-in="rise"><span class="im-card-title">Three</span></div>
	<div class="im-card" data-im-in="rise"><span class="im-card-title">Four</span></div>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Exits</h2>
<p>The way out, for a thing that is leaving: a toast dismissed, a card removed, a notice that has said its piece. Add the class, then remove or hide the element when the animation ends. An exit holds its last frame, so nothing flashes back before it goes.</p>
{{{{code "hbs"}}}}
<div class="im-toast im-out im-out-sink">…</div>
{{{{/code}}}}
{{{{code "js"}}}}
el.classList.add('im-out', 'im-out-sink');
const done = () => el.remove();
el.addEventListener('animationend', done, { once: true });
setTimeout(done, 600);   // an unpainted tab never ends an animation
{{{{/code}}}}
{{#example code=false}}
<div class="tiles tiles-3" data-replay>
