	<div class="tile" data-replay-tile><p class="im-caption" data-index="14">pixel</p><p class="text-h3 font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink im-out im-out-pixel" style="--im-out-delay: 600ms">On its way out.</p><span class="text-sm">Turns to Geist Pixel, then goes.</span></div>
</div>
{{/example}}
<p>Knobs: <code>--im-out-duration</code> (about 450ms — a way out is quicker than a way in), <code>--im-out-ease</code> (<code>--im-ease-in</code>), <code>--im-out-delay</code>, and <code>--im-i</code> for a stagger. Pair an exit with the entrance it mirrors: <code>rise</code> / <code>sink</code>, <code>wipe-up</code> / <code>wipe-down</code>, <code>unfold</code> / <code>fold</code>, <code>iris</code> / <code>iris</code>.</p>

<h2>Knobs</h2>
<div class="im-table-scroll">
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th></th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>--im-in-duration</code></td><td>How long. Defaults to <code>--im-duration-slow</code> (640ms); a few styles set their own.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>--im-in-ease</code></td><td>The curve. <code>--im-ease-out</code>.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>--im-in-delay</code></td><td>Wait before starting — for a hero: heading 0ms, lede 120ms, buttons 240ms.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>--im-in-steps</code></td><td><code>type</code>: how many steps. Roughly the number of characters.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>--im-in-curtain</code></td><td><code>curtain</code>: the panel's colour. The accent.</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h2>Choosing</h2>
<ul>
	<li><strong>One per kind, per site.</strong> A heading that rises on one page and flips on the next reads as a bug. Set the three variables and stop.</li>
	<li><strong>Quiet for many, loud for one.</strong> A grid of twenty cards wants <code>fade</code> or <code>rise</code>. <code>frame</code>, <code>curtain</code> and <code>pixel</code> are for the one thing at the top of the page.</li>
	<li><strong>Pairs that belong together:</strong> <code>line-up</code> + <code>wipe-up</code> + <code>unfold</code> (everything arrives through an edge) · <code>blur-in</code> + <code>develop</code> + <code>fade</code> (everything comes into focus).</li>
	<li><strong>Never delay reading.</strong> Body text does not get an entrance. Headings, pictures, cards and bands do.</li>
</ul>
